# requirements/relativity/einstein-1919.ears
capability: Einstein 1919 examination
owner: relativity
requirements:
  - id: REL-001
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The transcription module shall give every transcribed measurement an uncertainty convention and a page or table locator."
    rationale: "Transcription errors and convention confusion are the main integrity risks of UC-02. A row counts as verified after a recorded, matching second pass against the same locator; SDP is a single-user app, so the transcriber may make that pass (decided 2026-10-29). The latest pass decides: a correction made after a matching pass needs a matching pass of its own."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T1]
    gates: [REL-G-01]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_transcription::test_a_star_row_without_a_convention_is_refused"
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_transcription::test_every_star_row_carries_its_locator_and_convention"
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_protocol::test_a_star_row_without_a_locator_fails_the_link_gate"
  - id: REL-002
    pattern: unwanted
    text: "If a probable error enters a least-squares weight without explicit conversion, then the domain shall raise."
    rationale: "Probable errors quoted in 1920 overstate significance if used as standard errors."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T1]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_measurement::test_a_probable_error_cannot_become_a_weight_without_conversion"
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_measurement::test_the_conversion_is_explicit_and_named"
  - id: REL-003
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The relativity module shall take the physical constants of every deflection model from a recorded CODATA version."
    rationale: "The module never hard-codes 1.75 arcsec."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T1]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_models::test_changing_the_constants_changes_the_prediction"
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_models::test_limb_values_come_from_recorded_constants"
  - id: REL-004
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The relativity module shall fit each instrument set separately and pool them only under a PoolingJustification."
    rationale: "The instruments disagree; pooling hides that."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T1]
    gates: [REL-G-05]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_comparison::test_pooling_needs_a_stated_justification"
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_comparison::test_pooling_shares_alpha_and_keeps_plate_constants_per_instrument"
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_protocol::test_a_missing_instrument_counts_as_missing_hypotheses"
  - id: REL-005
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The module shall evaluate all four hypotheses per instrument and per scenario."
    rationale: "Competing hypotheses are compared on equal footing."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T8]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_comparison::test_every_hypothesis_is_evaluated_in_every_fit_scenario"
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_protocol::test_a_clean_synthetic_run_is_inconclusive_only_for_want_of_verified_oracles"
  - id: REL-006
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The sensitivity sweep shall cover the six predeclared scenario axes."
    rationale: "Conclusions must survive every predeclared reduction choice."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T8]
    gates: [REL-G-06]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_reduction::test_an_axis_value_the_module_does_not_implement_is_refused"
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_reduction::test_the_axes_are_the_six_predeclared_axes"
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_reduction::test_the_sweep_is_the_full_cross_product"
  - id: REL-007
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The fitter shall exist in two independent implementations that agree within tolerance."
    rationale: "Anything that issues a verdict is implemented twice."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T8]
    gates: [REL-G-08]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_independent::test_the_reference_fits_match_a_fresh_run"
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_protocol::test_an_independent_fitter_that_disagrees_fails_the_agreement_gate"
      - "typescript/packages/relativity-fit/test/fit.test.ts::[REL-007] agrees with the Python reference fitter on every instrument and scenario"
  - id: REL-008
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The dossier shall list unrecoverable inputs and describe a table-based reanalysis as a reanalysis, never as a plate remeasurement."
    rationale: "A table-based reanalysis is not a plate remeasurement."
    verification: test
    tiers: []
    gates: [REL-G-09]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_dossier::test_the_limitations_list_every_unrecoverable_input"
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_protocol::test_the_manifest_carries_the_limitations"
  - id: REL-009
    pattern: event
    text: "When the system builds the 1919 observation bundle from the transcribed 1920 tables, the system shall name every printed cell each row was built from, refuse a missing or unreadable cell by name, and mark rows verified only for a named verifier's recorded pass."
    rationale: "The 1920 report prints plate-against-plate measures, not deflections; each derived row must lead back to its cells on the page (REL-G-01) and must not count as checked until someone checked it (REL-G-02)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3]
    gates: [REL-G-01, REL-G-02, REL-G-04]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_paper1920::test_every_instrument_is_built_and_every_row_names_its_cells"
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_paper1920::test_the_sun_found_from_the_coefficients_gives_them_back"
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_paper1920::test_the_1920_reduction_reproduces_the_published_deflections"
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_paper1920::test_table_ii_agrees_with_the_1920_normal_equations_except_three_printed_cells"
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_paper1920::test_a_record_is_verified_only_when_every_cell_it_cites_was_checked"
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_paper1920::test_an_unchecked_plate_or_instrument_cell_withholds_every_star_fitted_with_it"
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_paper1920::test_only_a_recorded_check_counts_never_a_note_that_merely_contains_one"
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_paper1920::test_every_expected_measurement_must_be_transcribed_and_only_a_dash_means_none"
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_paper1920::test_a_missing_or_unreadable_cell_is_refused_by_name"
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_paper1920::test_the_1919_data_reproduces_the_published_values_and_waits_only_on_the_2020_reanalysis"
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_paper1920::test_every_cell_of_the_committed_transcription_has_a_recorded_check"
  - id: REL-010
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The fitter shall offer the 1920 reduction's six constants per plate as a plate model, subtract known linear terms and a known rotation when the scale is fixed, and solve a rotation the plate does not record."
    rationale: "The Sobral plates were reduced with independent x and y scales (p. 304), and differential refraction stretches one axis more than the other (p. 307), which one scale and one rotation cannot represent; orientation depends on how a plate sat in the measuring machine."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T6, T8]
    gates: [REL-G-04, REL-G-08]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_reduction::test_the_predeclared_historical_scenarios_are_the_ones_reproduced"
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_fitter::test_the_six_constant_model_absorbs_unequal_plate_scales"
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_fitter::test_a_set_measured_in_one_coordinate_leaves_the_other_constants_out"
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_fitter::test_fixed_scale_subtracts_known_terms_and_solves_an_unknown_rotation"
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_reduction::test_the_1920_reduction_differs_by_instrument_as_the_paper_describes"
      - "typescript/packages/relativity-fit/test/fit.test.ts::[REL-010] recovers alpha under the six-constant model when a plate's x and y scales differ"
      - "typescript/packages/relativity-fit/test/fit.test.ts::[REL-010] subtracts known terms and solves the rotation when the plate's orientation is unknown"
